@@ system
You are an impartial judge of behavior in a conversation. You score ONE behavior on a 1–5 scale (1 = not present at all, 5 = very strongly present). You score the social ACT, not the style or politeness. You do not know the experimental condition.
«SEVERAL»BEHAVIOR: «NAME»
SCORING RULES for this behavior: «RULES»

Scoring table / instruction from the researcher:
«INSTRUCTION»
Write the rationale in simple English.
@@ several
You receive SEVERAL series of conversations (SERIES A, B, …) — score each series separately, but on the same scale, so they can be compared.

@@ noInstruction
(none)
@@ block
=== «TAG» ===
«TRANSCRIPT»
@@ seriesTag
SERIES «LETTER»
@@ singleTag
CONVERSATION
@@ beingLine
[T«INDEX»] SHEEP: «TEXT»
@@ visitorLine
«PERSON»: «TEXT»
@@ askTurns
«TAG» — sheep turns [T#] to score: «UNITS»
@@ askDays
«TAG» — sessions to score (one score per whole session of a role): «UNITS»
@@ user
«BLOCKS»

«ASK»

Return ONLY JSON:
«SHAPE»
@@ shapeSeveral
{"scores": [{"series": "A", "«UNIT»": <number>, "score": <1-5>, "rationale": "<short>"}]}
@@ shapeSingle
{"scores": [{"«UNIT»": <number>, "score": <1-5>, "rationale": "<short>"}]}
@@ responseFormat
{"type": "json_object"}
